; === ACT 7: THE TIDE RACE ===
; The restored shelf drains to open sea, and the last stretch of the level is
; the water finding its way there. Appended rather than inserted: every
; coordinate in acts one to six is a number the flown route was measured
; against, and threading a new act through the middle would have moved all of
; them to add length at one end.
;
; It is also where the water is meant to be LOOKED at. Acts 2 and 4B cross
; water at depth, under a brow and under an arch, where the surface is
; overhead and mostly out of frame; here the route runs along the waterline
; for thirty metres with a bank either side, which is the one place in the
; level where the wave displacement, the surf against the shore and the splash
; going in are all in shot at once.
;
; Surfaces: landing 4.2, steps 3.4 and 2.6, the channel's own surface 2.6 so
; the last step walks straight in, the far shore 1.2 and the sea terrace 2.2.
; The sea shore sits SUBMERGED, six tenths of a metre under the waterline,
; for the same reason CoveShore does in act 2: a swimmer passes over a shore
; it can see the top of and settles onto it as the water runs out. A shore
; standing proud of the water is a wall you swim into, which is exactly what
; the flown route hit the first time this act was laid out.
; Every mandatory gap stays under 2.2 m and every mandatory rise under 1.2 m,
; the same envelope the rest of the level is built to.

