; === ACT 9: THE FLAGSHIP ===
; The end of the level, and the only boss in the game.
;
; Acts one to eight each taught something and then asked for it. This asks for
; all of it at once, against the vessel the whole fleet was launched from --
; and it is the LAST thing in the level, which is a design rule rather than a
; staging preference (REQ-013). Put a boss in the middle and everything after
; it is anticlimax; put it last and beating it is the payoff. Defeating this
; unlocks `open_sea`, the cores gathered through the yard are spent the moment
; it unlocks, the sea gate opens on `restored`, and the finish is past it: the
; restoration reward lands on the last thing the player did.
;
; THREE PHASES, ONE PER READ, and the hull is shaped so a player can see where
; the fight goes next before anyone explains it (REQ-013 AC-3, AC-4):
;
;   1. HULL BREACH, water only. Four intake mouths sit 1.9 m under the
;      waterline. The only way in is to swim, which is the grammar act 2
;      taught and the tide race asked for again.
;   2. DECK ASSAULT, land only. The deck stands 1.24 m proud of the water, so
;      boarding is a real transition rather than a swim-through, and the fight
;      on it is the land grammar with the tail whack.
;   3. CORE PURGE, gated on `bubble_platform`. The stern housing is shuttered;
;      the Bubble mod picked up in act 4 is what opens it. A player who never
;      collected it can reach this and not finish, which is the mod gate doing
;      its job.
;
; WHY IT IS BUILT AT LEVEL SCALE. Every other Drift Fleet machine is an
; obstacle a metre or two across. This one is a PLACE -- twenty-two metres of
; hull the player swims under, climbs onto and fights across -- so the mesh is
; generated at that scale and the collision below agrees with it rather than
; approximating it.

[node name="OpenSea" type="Area3D" parent="."]
