; NINE FLEET CORES against a cost of seven, so the economy has two spare.
; Laid out at exactly seven first, and the flown route collected six: one
; pickup sat two metres off the line between a landing and a fight, and with
; no slack that single miss made the level unfinishable. Act 6's kelp seeds
; are still exactly seven against seven and that is the reason its Dredger has
; to stand outside the seed bed; this act does not repeat the constraint.
;
; The original seven were placed on the yard's landings because`open_sea` costs (3 to resourced,
; 4 to restored, this world's overridden costs). They are gathered through
; the yard while the region is still locked -- banked, not spent -- and the
; Flagship's defeat spends them all at once. That is the payoff landing on
; the fight rather than on an errand.
;
; Placed ON the yard's landings rather than between them. Laid out mid-arc
; first and the flown route sailed past several of them: a pickup a jump
; passes through at speed is a pickup the player misses, and with an economy
; this tight one missed core is a level that cannot be finished.
[node name="FleetCore1" type="Area3D" parent="." groups=["collectible"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 4.2, -218)
metadata/collectible_id = "fleet_core"

