; === DRIFT FLEET ===
; ON THE ROUTE, NOT BESIDE IT. Every machine used to stand six to ten metres
; off the line the level is designed around, and the longest strike reaches
; 2.3 m: the whole combat lane was unreachable in play. A player walking the
; route swam past all four and never met one. These stand where the route
; goes.
;
; ONE LADDER, CLIMBED IN ORDER. The first machine a player meets is the
; one-hit Netbot, in water, where a single spin sprint both frees them from
; its net and ends it -- the cheapest possible place to learn that machines
; can be hit at all. From there the count rises: two-strike Rigs on land once
; the Glow mod makes their lines visible, three-strike Drones fought from
; inside their own murk, and the four-strike Dredger guarding the seed bed it
; exists to undo. Nothing is introduced at a durability the player has not
; already seen one step below.
;
; MATCHED TO THE GRAMMAR THEY STAND IN. Water machines are met swimming, where
; the strike verb is the spin sprint; land machines are met on foot, where it
; is the tail whack. A machine placed across a grammar boundary would be a
; machine the player fights with a verb the level never taught them there.
;
; EACH IS ITS OWN UNIT. The runtime keys defeat by placed node, so the three
; Netbots below are three separate fights: beating the one in the lagoon
; leaves the one in the tide race standing.

; --- Act 2: the lagoon. Two Netbots, the teaching pair. -----------------------
[node name="NetbotLagoonGap" type="Area3D" parent="." groups=["enemy"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -5, -37.6)
metadata/enemy_id = "netbot"

[node name="Model" parent="NetbotLagoonGap" instance=ExtResource("20_fleet_netbot")]

[node name="Collision" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="NetbotLagoonGap"]
shape = SubResource("BoxShape3D_80")

; The second arrives mid-climb over RiseWall, so the lesson is repeated
; under a little pressure rather than at rest.
[node name="NetbotRiseWall" type="Area3D" parent="." groups=["enemy"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0.6, -43.6)
metadata/enemy_id = "netbot"

[node name="Model" parent="NetbotRiseWall" instance=ExtResource("20_fleet_netbot")]

[node name="Collision" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="NetbotRiseWall"]
shape = SubResource("BoxShape3D_80")


; --- Act 4: the grotto. Rigs, once Glow can reveal their lines. ---------------
; On the wall top with the Glow mod already in hand and the gate ahead, so the
; player fights it able to SEE its line -- which is the whole of the Glow
; counter. Off to one side of the top rather than astride the jump to pillar
; one: the gap past the gate is 2.6 m, the widest on the route, and a machine
; standing in it would be a machine that has to be fought from mid-air.
[node name="HooklineGlowGate" type="Area3D" parent="." groups=["enemy"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3.2, 8.2, -67.4)
